From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: hit-test the release of a caption right click with WM_NCHITTEST

Purpose: open the taskbar menu when the unlocked XP taskbar is right
clicked between its bands.
XP behavior: WM_CONTEXTMENU follows the release of the right button in the
caption, as documented for WM_NCRBUTTONUP. The taskbar has no WS_CAPTION
but its own WM_NCHITTEST returns HTCAPTION there, so that it can be dragged.
Wine before: DefWindowProc entered the WM_NCRBUTTONDOWN loop for HTCAPTION
but hit-tested the release with its internal default, which only knows
WS_CAPTION windows, got HTCLIENT and sent no WM_CONTEXTMENU.
Change: ask the window with WM_NCHITTEST, as for the button press.
Evidence: tests/nc-context-menu.c covers a captionless popup that returns
HTCAPTION.
Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/menurc/wm-contextmenu
Scope: documented behaviour, for every Wine application.
Old patches: 0047.
---
 dlls/win32u/defwnd.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
index a1b6d1d..7f5d0a4 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
@@ -2263,7 +2263,10 @@ static LRESULT handle_nc_rbutton_down( HWND hwnd, WPARAM wparam, LPARAM lparam )
             if (NtUserCallMsgFilter( &msg, MSGF_MAX )) continue;
             if (msg.message == WM_RBUTTONUP)
             {
-                hittest = handle_nc_hit_test( hwnd, msg.pt );
+                /* Ask the window, as the button-down hit test did. A window
+                 * without WS_CAPTION may return HTCAPTION from its own
+                 * WM_NCHITTEST, as the unlocked XP taskbar does. */
+                hittest = send_message( hwnd, WM_NCHITTEST, 0, MAKELPARAM( msg.pt.x, msg.pt.y ));
                 break;
             }
         }
